  "title": "ConTrack: Constrained Hand Motion Tracking with Adaptive Trade-off Control",
  "title_zh": "ConTrack：具有自适应权衡控制的约束手部运动跟踪",
  "abstract": "Human demonstrations provide strong priors for robot manipulation, yet it is non-trivial to transfer them to execute on real robots due to the kinematic gap. In dexterous manipulation, it remains challenging to track long-horizon, contact-rich sequences even in simulators: a reference-tracking policy must keep objects on their target trajectories while preserving demonstrated joint motion and contact timing. Existing approaches often rely on hand-crafted reward tuning that require per-sequence t",
